    title="Compare two camera-based mower capacities"
    intro="First confirm your grass, boundaries and daylight mowing window. Compare these eufy models only for mostly flat, clearly bounded lawns: neither suits buffalo (St. Augustine) or dense Zoysia. Both adjust from 25–75 mm. Their 800 m² and 1,200 m² limits describe map size, not coverage on one charge."
  />
  <p>Both offers were available from AnkerDirect AU through Amazon Australia when checked on 13 September 2026. Check the seller and delivery postcode again before ordering. Neither model removes edge trimming, obstacle clearing or the need to supervise the first runs.</p>

  <h2>Plan safety before setting a schedule</h2>
  <p>Keep children, pets and other people out of the mowing area during operation. Clear toys, hoses, fallen branches and animal waste. Check for wildlife before starting and choose daylight mowing windows that avoid times animals use the lawn. Sensors are not a guarantee that every animal or small object will be detected.</p>
  <p>Ask the installer to assess ponds, drops, driveways and public access, including required barriers and setbacks. Do not rely on a virtual boundary as a physical safety barrier. Follow the shutdown procedure and wait for blades to stop before lifting, clearing or maintaining the mower.</p>
  <p>Check the exact model and serial number in <a href="https://www.productsafety.gov.au/recalls" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ACCC Product Safety’s recall database</a>, including for second-hand purchases. Use the specified battery and charging equipment; <a href="https://www.fire.nsw.gov.au/fire-safety/home-fire-safety/battery-and-charging-safety/shop-charge-and-recycle-safely" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fire and Rescue NSW explains battery purchasing, charging and disposal precautions</a>.</p>

  <h2>Price the installation and the work that remains</h2>
  <p>Have the supplier itemise boundary equipment, station placement, mapping, any antenna and electrical work. Check a suitable power supply position, docking clearance, drainage, sun exposure and protection of cables. Do not assume the mower, power supply and station share the same weather rating.</p>
  <p>Allow for blades, battery replacement, servicing, electricity, optional connectivity subscriptions and repairs. Establish who services the exact Australian model locally, written warranty terms and how repairs are transported. Ask which app functions require an account or cloud connection and how long software support is promised.</p>
  <p>Compare that total with keeping your mower or using a lawn service, including remaining edge trimming and obstacle clearing. Frequent carrying between small lawns may erode the time saved.</p>

  <h2>Before you buy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Record actual lawn areas, passage widths and slopes with their units.</li>
    <li>Confirm navigation, grass height and capacity for your available mowing hours.</li>
    <li>Resolve hazards, station placement and installation requirements.</li>
    <li>Get the complete quote, maintenance costs and service arrangements in writing.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><a href="/downloads/robot-lawn-mower-yard-assessment.pdf" download>Print the A4 yard-assessment worksheet</a> and take your sketch and unresolved questions to the supplier before ordering.</p>

